    "faq": {
      "type": "faq",
      "settings": {
        "label": "Questions",
        "title": "The obvious ones"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need the kit to use Clippar?",
            "answer": "<p>No. The app is free and it works with any phone mount you already own, or propped against your bag if you're feeling brave.</p><p>The kit exists because the fiddly parts — something that actually grips a buggy rail, a clicker you don't have to hold, and a battery that survives eighteen holes of filming — are the difference between doing this once and doing it every week.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need an iPhone?",
            "answer": "<p><strong>Yes.</strong> Clippar is iOS only and there's no Android version yet. The mount will hold an Android phone quite happily, but nothing will detect or clip your shots.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is this a swing coach?",
            "answer": "<p>No, and it isn't trying to be. It makes no claim about your technique and it won't tell you what you did wrong.</p><p>It films the shot that already happened and gives you the footage. What you do with that is your business.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "When does the kit ship?",
            "answer": "<p>December 2026 is the target for the first production run. You can cancel any time before dispatch for a full refund — if the date moves, you'll hear it from us first.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does it slow the group down?",
            "answer": "<p>It shouldn't. The phone stays on the bag and the clicker stays on your belt, so filming a shot is one press before and one press after.</p><p>There's nothing to set up on each tee and nothing to pack away between holes.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does it cost to keep using?",
            "answer": "<p>Nothing. Recording, shot detection, trimming and saving to your camera roll are free forever.</p><p>Clippar Pro is optional and adds cloud backup so your rounds survive a lost phone. You never need it.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
